gcm/live-draw: RSX_INTERNAL_SCALE=2 renders live-draw at twice the guest's resolution per axis (experimental); FSR 1
is refused while it is on; the present draws the scaled image.

Purpose (issue #55, step 2): turn on the fixed-2x path that patch 2302 prepared. ENHANCEMENT, opt-in: unset (the
default) or 1 renders as before. The number follows the 6xxx block because the FSR 1 option (6051), the pre-HUD tap
(6052) and the present (6055) apply after the 2300-2319 block reserved for this series; the maintainer was asked in
issue #55 to name another number if this one collides.

Change (libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c):
- ld_iscale_activate() makes the switch's scale (2301) the live scale, once at start, before any host resource.
- ld_up_get: FSR 1 and the internal scale are exclusive for now (no silent double scaling; FSR/XeSS are to sit on the
  internal scale later). Checked every frame, so the Display page's UPSCALING row (6051) and RSX_UPSCALE_AB cannot
  turn it on at 2x; without it the pre-HUD tap (6052) never runs. One "[upscale] ... refused" line per choice.
- Present: a scaled image is never the back buffer's size, so it is always drawn by 2095's display pass (bilinear:
  at a 2:1 window the filter is an exact 2x2 box), never copied; the letterbox rectangle is the guest-size image's,
  which the cursor mapping (rsx_null_backend.c) assumes. If the draw cannot be recorded the frame is not shown and
  logged ("[iscale] present: ..."), instead of a CopyResource of mismatched sizes.
- The [iscale] start line says the scale is active.

Known limits (also docs/KNOWN_ISSUES.md): no menu row (environment only); 1x and 2x only; FSR 1 off at 2x; whatever
the game composes on the SPUs from a written-back surface (its post chain) is at the guest's resolution and expanded;
pipeline templates are prewarmed but not written at 2x.

Verification: tools/runtime/test_internal_scale_map.sh: header (2x extents, composed scissor and clear, the scaled
WPOS formula for every texel of 4096, report-count rounding and saturation) and wiring (allocation, every guest
boundary through the guards, the scale keyed only when not 1x, FSR refused at 2x, the switch read once). A negative
control on the tree without 2302/6082 fails every wiring check. rsx_live_draw.c compiled with MinGW-w64 gcc 16.2 at
-O2 -Wall -Wextra with no new diagnostics. Native Windows 11, first-run build with the bundled llvm-mingw (7 steps,
438 s), US 1.29: a 120 s scripted run at 2x reached the main menu with the presented surface dumped at 2560x1440
(correct picture); hand play of the same build at 2x (~8,000 frames) and at 1x (~7,800 frames), both ended by Exit to
desktop with exit code 0, no D3D errors; at 2x the player saw no artefacts or lighting problems. At 2x the write-back
guard ran on two main-memory surfaces every frame (640x360 RGBA8 box, 320x180 R32F one texel); no guest upload into a
scaled surface was seen. Whole-run 5 s fps samples (menus included, not the same path): mean 43.8 at 2x, 47.7 at 1x;
no same-scene frame times yet.

Written for this port; not taken from RPCS3 or any other emulator.

